Who defines "broken"? Is my newsreader broken because it doesn't reorder
top-posted comments into a more readable order, or because it doesn't trim
excessive material? Am I "control freaking" if I ask someone not to
top-post? I'm just curious - where do you draw the line?

I'd say RFCs would be a good place. Show me an RFC that demands subject
lines be displayed on the same screen as message bodies, and I'll acquiesce
to you. Also, consider a newsreader which puts the subject line on a status
bar at the bottom of the screen. I wouldn't consider that a broken design at
all - but it would make reading the OP less than natural.

I don't feel particularly strongly one way or another here, to be honest,
because my newsreader displays things in a way I can understand; but I try
to post so that others can understand too. I feel people have every right to
say "I have difficulty reading your news because of the way you post, and
I'd appreciate it if you changed your ways". Of course, people are often
less polite than that, which is where it spins out of control...

